{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170785766,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010d30001iSPLJ3V7lJV821","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_8bb1fe3d5d7d45cb91eecc1c","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore Game component UI controls","prompt":"Explore the Game component to understand what UI controls are currently implemented. I need to find:\n1. What buttons are present (PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR)?\n2. What interaction mode buttons are present (DRAW, ERASE)?\n3. What status controls are present (waveform, volume, generation)?\n4. What's the current UI structure?\n\nReturn a detailed summary of the current UI controls in the Game component."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef2b7ffeLsYNupsIYlHLER (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Detailed Summary of UI Controls in Game Component\n\nBased on my analysis of `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`, here's what I found:\n\n### 1. Buttons Present\n\n**Main Control Buttons:**\n- **Start/Running** (lines 80-82): Acts as the PLAY/PAUSE equivalent. Shows \"Start\" in PLANNING phase, disabled when running or if no cells are alive\n- **Clear** (lines 83-85): Clears the entire grid and resets to PLANNING phase, only available in PLANNING phase\n- **Random** (lines 86-88): Randomly fills the grid with cells (15% density) and resets to PLANNING phase, only available in PLANNING phase\n\n**Grid Size Buttons:**\n- **Small** (lines 66-68): Sets grid to small preset (20x30)\n- **Medium** (lines 69-71): Sets grid to medium preset\n- **Large** (lines 72-74): Sets grid to large preset\n\n**Grid Visibility Button:**\n- **Hide Grid / Show Grid** (lines 94-96): Toggles grid lines visibility, only available in PLANNING phase\n\n### 2. Interaction Mode Buttons\n\n**Present:**\n- **Draw** (lines 102-108): Sets interaction mode to DRAW, highlighted in cyan (#61dafb) when active, only available in PLANNING phase\n- **Erase** (lines 109-115): Sets interaction mode to ERASE, highlighted in cyan when active, only available in PLANNING phase\n\n### 3. Status Controls\n\n**Present:**\n- **Phase** (line 130): Displays current game phase (PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, etc.)\n- **Cells** (line 131): Displays the count of alive cells in the grid\n- **Flux** (lines 132-138): Displays current flux value with color-coded status:\n  - Green when > 10\n  - Orange when > 5\n  - Red when ≤ 5\n\n**NOT Present:**\n- ❌ **STEP button**: No single-step button implemented\n- ❌ **Waveform control**: No waveform selection or visualization controls\n- ❌ **Volume control**: No volume slider or audio controls\n- ❌ **Generation counter**: No generation count display\n\n### 4. Current UI Structure\n\nThe UI is organized in the following vertical sections:\n\n1. **Header** (lines 58-60): Title \"Conway's Game of Life\" with cyan color\n\n2. **Control Button Groups** (lines 62-117):\n   - Grid size selector row\n   - Main game control buttons (Start, Clear, Random)\n   - Grid visibility toggle\n   - Interaction mode toggle (Draw/Erase)\n\n3. **Status Display Bar** (lines 119-140):\n   - Dark semi-transparent background with blur effect\n   - Shows Phase, Cells count, and Flux value\n\n4. **Grid Interaction Area** (lines 142-152):\n   - The GridInteraction component that renders the actual game grid\n\n**Key Behavioral Notes:**\n- Most controls are disabled during game phases other than PLANNING\n- All buttons use inline styles rather than CSS classes\n- The interaction mode buttons provide visual feedback by changing background color when active\n- The Start button text changes based on game phase\n</task_result>","title":"Explore Game component UI controls","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef2b7ffeLsYNupsIYlHLER","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170762052,"end":1771170785764}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170809129,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010cc2001l72llIzvNPtoTx","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_0dabf9573de74933aa8346cb","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore GlassHUD implementation status","prompt":"Explore the GlassHUD component implementation in src/components/GlassHUD.tsx. I need to understand:\n1. What is currently implemented?\n2. What buttons/controls are present?\n3. What's missing compared to the spec in specs/ui-overlay.md?\n4. Are there any test files for GlassHUD?\n\nReturn a detailed summary of the current implementation status and what's missing."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef335ffejkfeKYS1Z9CkW6 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my analysis of the GlassHUD component and its specification, here's a detailed summary:\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Summary: GlassHUD Implementation Status\n\n### 1. Currently Implemented Features\n\n**GlassHUD.tsx Structure:**\n- **Props Interface**: Receives `phase`, `aliveCount`, `flux`, `fluxMax`, `interactionMode`, `gridPreset`, `showGridLines`, `canStart`, `canInteract`, and 8 callback handlers\n- **Status Display** (Lines 126-139): Shows Phase, Cells (alive count), and Flux with color-coded values\n- **Flux Color Coding** (Lines 42-48): \n  - Red when flux <= 0\n  - Orange when flux < 0.5\n  - Green when flux >= 0.5\n\n**Control Groups:**\n\n| Group | Buttons/Controls | Location |\n|-------|------------------|----------|\n| Main Controls | START/RUNNING, RANDOM, CLEAR | Lines 56-74 |\n| Interaction Modes | DRAW, ERASE | Lines 76-91 |\n| Grid Size | Small, Medium, Large | Lines 93-115 |\n| Utilities | Show/Hide Grid, Settings (⚙️) | Lines 117-124 |\n\n### 2. Buttons/Controls Present\n\n**Main Control Buttons:**\n- ✓ **START/RUNNING**: Toggles text based on phase\n- ✓ **RANDOM**: Fills grid randomly (disabled when `canInteract` is false)\n- ✓ **CLEAR**: Clears grid with danger styling (red text)\n\n**Interaction Mode Buttons:**\n- ✓ **DRAW**: Highlights when active (`interactionMode === 'DRAW'`)\n- ✓ **ERASE**: Highlights when active (`interactionMode === 'ERASE'`)\n\n**Grid Size Buttons:**\n- ✓ **Small**: For `gridPreset === 'SMALL'`\n- ✓ **Medium**: For `gridPreset === 'MEDIUM'`\n- ✓ **Large**: For `gridPreset === 'LARGE'`\n\n**Utility Controls:**\n- ✓ **Grid Toggle**: Shows \"Show Grid\" or \"Hide Grid\" based on `showGridLines`\n- ✓ **Settings Toggle**: Gear icon (⚙️)\n\n**Status Display:**\n- ✓ Phase display (PLANNING, RUNNING, etc.)\n- ✓ Alive cells count\n- ✓ Flux value with color coding\n\n### 3. Missing Features Compared to Spec (specs/ui-overlay.md)\n\n#### **Critical Missing Features:**\n\n| Feature | Spec Requirement | Status |\n|---------|------------------|--------|\n| **STEP Button** | Execute single generation, disabled while running | ❌ Missing |\n| **PLAY/PAUSE Button** | Toggle simulation running state | ❌ Currently START/RUNNING (different behavior) |\n| **Generation Counter** | Display \"GEN: {number}\" | ❌ Missing |\n| **Waveform Selector** | Dropdown (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw) | ❌ Missing |\n| **Volume Slider** | Range 0-0.5, 0.01 step | ❌ Missing |\n\n#### **Settings Panel Features (should be in SettingsPanel, not GlassHUD):**\n- Speed slider (10ms to 500ms)\n- Grid size configuration (currently in HUD, should be in Settings according to spec)\n- Show grid lines checkbox\n- Audio sonification checkbox\n- Expert Settings access button\n\n#### **Phase Status Display Issues:**\n- ✓ Phase display is implemented\n- ❌ **Timer display**: Missing (should be visible during COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases)\n- ✓ Flux counter implemented (visible during PLANNING and RUNNING phases)\n\n### 4. Test File Status\n\n**Test Coverage**: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.test.tsx`\n\n**Existing Tests (19 tests total):**\n- ✓ Render all control groups (5 assertions)\n- ✓ Render status display (5 assertions)\n- ✓ onStart button click handler\n- ✓ onRandom button click handler\n- ✓ onClear button click handler\n- ✓ onSetMode for DRAW/ERASE\n- ✓ onSetGridPreset for Medium/Large\n- ✓ onToggleGrid handler\n- ✓ onToggleSettings handler\n- ✓ Disable interactions when `canInteract` is false (7 assertions)\n- ✓ Disable START when `canStart` is false\n- ✓ Grid toggle text changes\n- ✓ Flux color coding (3 assertions)\n- ✓ Active mode highlighting\n- ✓ Active grid preset highlighting\n- ✓ Phase-based button text change\n\n**Test Coverage Gaps:**\n- No tests for missing features (STEP button, generation counter, waveform selector, volume slider)\n- No tests for Small grid preset button\n- No tests for all grid buttons in one test\n- No tests for edge cases (empty states, invalid values)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Implementation Progress**: Approximately **60-65% complete**\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Core HUD structure is solid with glass effect styling\n- Basic game controls (START, RANDOM, CLEAR, DRAW, ERASE) work\n- Grid size selection is functional\n- Good test coverage for implemented features\n\n**Critical Gaps:**\n1. **Missing STEP button** for single-generation execution\n2. **Missing Generation counter** (GEN: {number})\n3. **Missing Audio controls** (waveform selector, volume slider)\n4. **Missing Timer display** for countdown/running phases\n5. **Settings architecture mismatch** - grid size buttons should be in Settings panel per spec\n\n**Recommended Next Steps:**\n1. Add STEP button to main controls\n2. Add generation counter to status display (requires new prop)\n3. Add timer display for COUNTDOWN/RUNNING phases\n4. Move grid size buttons to SettingsPanel component\n5. Create SettingsPanel with speed, volume, and audio controls\n6. Add tests for new features\n</task_result>","title":"Explore GlassHUD implementation status","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef335ffejkfeKYS1Z9CkW6","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170761928,"end":1771170809127}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170827376,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010ccc001zA39qkhvBwoj5g","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_c963731944194c7e8b56f7e7","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore phase display UI status","prompt":"Explore where phase status is displayed in the current codebase. I need to find:\n1. Where is the current phase (PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED) displayed?\n2. Is there a timer display for COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases?\n3. Is there a Flux counter display?\n4. Are these implemented in the Game component or elsewhere?\n\nReturn the location of these displays and their implementation status."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef327ffeNXYeH7zSMc03YT (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my exploration of the codebase, here's what I found regarding phase status displays:\n\n## 1. Phase Display Location and Implementation\n\n### Where is the current phase displayed?\n\n**In Game.tsx** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`)\n- **Line 130**: `<div>Phase: {phase}</div>`\n- Displays the phase as plain text in a simple status bar\n- Shows: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, or FINISHED\n\n**In GlassHUD.tsx** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`)\n- **Lines 128-129**: Displays phase with label formatting\n```tsx\n<span className=\"hud-status-label\">Phase:</span>\n<span className=\"hud-status-value\">{phase}</span>\n```\n- Part of a glass-morphism styled HUD component (currently not integrated with Game.tsx)\n\n## 2. Timer Display Status\n\n### Countdown Timer (COUNTDOWN phase)\n- **Status**: NOT DISPLAYED\n- **Logic exists** in `lib/phase.ts` (lines 5, 50, 87-100):\n  - `countdownValue` field stores the countdown value\n  - `DECREMENT_COUNTDOWN` action decrements it\n  - Starts at `COUNTDOWN_SECONDS` (3 seconds)\n- **No visual representation** in Game.tsx or GlassHUD.tsx\n\n### Running Timer (RUNNING phase)\n- **Status**: NOT DISPLAYED\n- **Logic exists** in `lib/phase.ts` (lines 6, 111, 117-136):\n  - `timerRemaining` field stores remaining time\n  - `DECREMENT_TIMER` action decrements it\n  - Set by `START_RUNNING` action with a duration parameter\n- **No visual representation** in Game.tsx or GlassHUD.tsx\n\n## 3. Flux Counter Display\n\n**In Game.tsx** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`)\n- **Lines 132-138**: Implemented with color coding\n```tsx\n<div style={{\n  color: flux.current > 10 ? '#00ff00' : flux.current > 5 ? '#ffaa00' : '#ff0000',\n}}>\n  Flux: {flux.current}\n</div>\n```\n- Thresholds: Green (>10), Orange (6-10), Red (≤5)\n\n**In GlassHUD.tsx** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`)\n- **Lines 135-138**: More sophisticated color coding\n```tsx\n<span className=\"hud-status-label\">Flux:</span>\n<span className={`hud-status-value ${fluxColor}`}>{flux}</span>\n```\n- Uses `getFluxColor()` function (lines 42-48) based on ratio (green/orange/red)\n\n## 4. Component Implementation Location\n\n### Game.tsx\n- **Primary implementation** currently in use\n- Simple HTML-based status display\n- Lines 119-140: Status bar showing Phase, Cells, and Flux\n- Does NOT use the phase reducer or display timers\n\n### GlassHUD.tsx\n- **Secondary/polished implementation**\n- Glass-morphism styled component with proper CSS classes\n- Includes Phase, Cells, and Flux displays\n- Better visual presentation with CSS classes and color coding\n- **Not currently integrated** - Game.tsx doesn't render this component\n\n## Summary\n\n| Feature | Game.tsx | GlassHUD.tsx | Implementation Status |\n|---------|----------|--------------|----------------------|\n| Phase Display | ✅ Line 130 | ✅ Lines 128-129 | **IMPLEMENTED** in both |\n| Countdown Timer | ❌ | ❌ | Logic exists, **NOT DISPLAYED** |\n| Running Timer | ❌ | ❌ | Logic exists, **NOT DISPLAYED** |\n| Flux Counter | ✅ Lines 132-138 | ✅ Lines 135-138 | **IMPLEMENTED** in both |\n\n### Key Findings:\n- The phase display is fully implemented in both components\n- Timer logic exists in `lib/phase.ts` but no UI displays it\n- Flux counter is fully implemented with color coding in both components\n- GlassHUD.tsx is a more polished version but isn't being used in the current Game component\n- The Game component doesn't use the PhaseState type or phaseReducer, so timer values aren't tracked or displayed\n</task_result>","title":"Explore phase display UI status","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef327ffeNXYeH7zSMc03YT","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170761942,"end":1771170827373}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170836318,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010cfb001qb2lZ7A86mc3xa","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_312c631b132440739f4cc402","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore transition system implementation","prompt":"Explore if a transition system has been implemented for level transitions. I need to check:\n1. Is there a transitions.ts file in src/lib/?\n2. Are there any transition state or animations implemented?\n3. Does the game have fade in/out effects between levels?\n4. Are there any transition components?\n\nReturn a detailed summary of transition system implementation status."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef2f1ffeNSTTzUtxacml0Y (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's a detailed summary of the transition system implementation status:\n\n---\n\n## Transition System Implementation Status Report\n\n### 1. **transitions.ts File in src/lib/**\n**Status: ❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n- No `transitions.ts` file exists in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/`\n- The file is listed as a future implementation task in Sprint 3.2 of the Implementation Plan\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Transition State and Animations**\n\n#### **Type Definitions (✅ DEFINED ONLY)**\nThe transition system types are defined in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nexport type TransitionState = 'PLAYING' | 'FADING_OUT' | 'INTERSTITIAL' | 'FADING_IN' | 'READY'\n\nexport interface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: number\n  fadeInDuration: number\n  interstitialDuration: number\n  autoAdvanceDelay: number\n  skipEnabled: boolean\n}\n```\n\nHowever, **these types are not used anywhere** in the codebase. They are defined but have no implementation.\n\n#### **Current Animation State (❌ NO LEVEL TRANSITIONS)**\nThe only animations implemented are:\n- **IntroOverlay exit animation**: `fadeInScaleOut` (1.2s) in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/IntroOverlay.css`\n- **Intro glitch effect**: CSS keyframe animations for title text\n- **Button hover effects**: Standard CSS transitions in GlassHUD and IntroOverlay\n\n**No fade in/out effects between levels exist.**\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Fade In/Out Effects Between Levels**\n**Status: ❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\nThe specification requires:\n- Fade out (2.0s) - Full-screen black overlay opacity 0→1\n- Interstitial (2.0s) - Black screen with level info\n- Fade in (2.0s) - Black overlay opacity 1→0\n\n**Current implementation:**\n- No full-screen overlay component for level transitions\n- No opacity transition animations for level changes\n- No interstitial display component\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Transition Components**\n**Status: ❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\nNo transition-related components exist:\n- No `TransitionOverlay` component\n- No `LevelInterstitial` component  \n- No `VictoryScreen` component (planned for Sprint 3.3)\n- No skip indicator component\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Level Progression Status**\n**Status: ❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\nThe types are defined:\n```typescript\nexport interface LevelConfig {\n  levelNumber: number\n  timeLimitSeconds: number\n  initialFlux: number\n}\n\nexport interface LevelProgression {\n  currentLevel: number\n  maxUnlockedLevel: number\n  totalScore: number\n  levels: LevelConfig[]\n}\n```\n\n**However, level progression is not implemented:**\n- No `level.ts` file in `src/lib/`\n- No level state management in any components\n- The `Game` component only has single-level gameplay\n- No level display UI\n- No level completion detection\n- No level advancement logic\n\n---\n\n### 6. **What IS Implemented**\n\n#### **Phase Management** (✅ COMPLETE)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.ts` - Fully implemented\n- Game phases: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED → PLANNING\n- Phase state machine with guarded transitions\n- Timer management for COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases\n- **Note**: Phase transitions work within a single level, but do NOT trigger level progression\n\n#### **Intro Transition** (✅ COMPLETE)\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/IntroOverlay.tsx`\n- 1.2s fade/scale exit animation\n- \"ENTER VOID\" button triggers transition\n- Works as a one-time intro sequence, not level transitions\n\n#### **CSS Transitions** (✅ PARTIAL)\n- Button hover effects (0.2s - 0.5s)\n- Intro exit animation (1.2s)\n- Ghost cell preview opacity (0.5)\n- No level transition animations\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Specifications Status**\n\n#### **auto-advance-transitions.md** (❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED)\nThe specification calls for:\n- Transition state machine with 5 states\n- Fade out → interstitial → fade in sequence\n- Skip functionality (Space/ESC)\n- Audio for transitions\n- Browser tab handling during transitions\n\n**None of this is implemented.**\n\n#### **level-progression.md** (❌ NOT IMPLEMENTED)\nThe specification calls for:\n- Level configuration generation\n- Difficulty scaling\n- Level display UI\n- Victory screen after final level\n\n**None of this is implemented.**\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Implementation Plan Status**\n\nFrom `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`:\n\n**Sprint 3: Level Progression & Transitions** - Status: ❌ NOT STARTED\n\n- **3.1 Level Progression**: Not implemented\n- **3.2 Transition System**: Not implemented (transitions.ts file)\n- **3.3 Victory Screen**: Not implemented\n\nThe implementation plan shows this is scheduled for Week 4 (Days 17-18).\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Codebase Statistics**\n\n- **Total TypeScript/TSX files**: 18 files (excluding node_modules)\n- **Total lines of code**: ~4,289 lines\n- **Components with transitions**: 1 (IntroOverlay)\n- **Lib files**: 18 files (0 for transitions or levels)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe transition system for level transitions is **NOT IMPLEMENTED**. While type definitions exist (`TransitionState`, `TransitionConfig`, `LevelConfig`, `LevelProgression`), there is no actual implementation:\n\n1. **No transitions.ts file** in src/lib/\n2. **No transition state machine** implemented\n3. **No fade in/out effects** between levels\n4. **No transition components** exist\n5. **No level progression** system implemented\n6. **Only intro transition** exists (one-time entry animation)\n\nThe game currently operates as a single-level experience with phase transitions (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED) but does not advance to new levels. Level progression and cinematic level transitions remain as planned features for Sprint 3.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore transition system implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef2f1ffeNSTTzUtxacml0Y","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170761995,"end":1771170836312}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170861020,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010d140012VROQxrQzonYqC","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_d5e400008eaf492baf5f1b7c","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore cell animations implementation","prompt":"Explore if cell animations are implemented. I need to check:\n1. Do cells have fade-in animations when placed?\n2. Do cells have shrink animations when removed?\n3. Is there a red flash for invalid actions?\n4. Are these animations implemented in CSS or canvas?\n\nReturn a detailed summary of cell animation implementation status."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef2d6ffe5Zm8B39Zp6e53B (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's a detailed summary of cell animation implementation status:\n\n## Cell Animation Implementation Status Summary\n\n### 1. Fade-in Animations When Cells Are Placed\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n- **Required by spec**: \"Cell Placement: Fade-in animation (0.1s duration)\" (specs/grid-interaction.md line 39)\n- **Required by spec**: \"Cell appears with fade-in animation\" (specs/flux-management.md line 52)\n- **Current implementation**: In `GridInteraction.tsx` lines 52-58, when a cell is placed, the code simply sets the grid value directly:\n  ```typescript\n  const newGrid = grid.map((r, rIdx) =>\n    r.map((cell, cIdx) => (rIdx === row && cIdx === col ? 1 : cell))\n  )\n  ```\n- **No animation framework or transition logic exists** for cell placement\n- **Implementation plan** marks this as TODO (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md lines 235-238, 632-635)\n\n### 2. Shrink Animations When Cells Are Removed\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n- **Required by spec**: \"Cell Removal: Shrink animation (0.15s duration)\" (specs/grid-interaction.md line 40)\n- **Required by spec**: \"Cell shrinks and disappears\" (specs/flux-management.md line 55)\n- **Current implementation**: In `GridInteraction.tsx` lines 42-49, when a cell is removed, the code simply sets the cell to 0:\n  ```typescript\n  const newGrid = grid.map((r, rIdx) =>\n    r.map((cell, cIdx) => (rIdx === row && cIdx === col ? 0 : cell))\n  )\n  ```\n- **No animation framework or transition logic exists** for cell removal\n- **Implementation plan** marks this as TODO (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md lines 235-238, 632-635)\n\n### 3. Red Flash for Invalid Actions\n**Status: PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED (Static visual feedback, not animated flash)**\n\n- **Required by spec**: \"Invalid Action: Brief red flash on cursor location\" (specs/grid-interaction.md line 41)\n- **Required by spec**: \"Visual: Brief red flash on Flux counter\" (specs/flux-management.md line 49)\n- **Current implementation**: In `GridInteraction.tsx` line 168, there's a static red border when Flux is 0:\n  ```typescript\n  border: `2px solid ${isPlaceable() ? '#00ffff' : isRemovable() ? '#ff00ff' : '#ff0000'}`,\n  ```\n- This is a **static border color change**, not a flashing animation\n- The ghost cell preview shows red when placement is not possible (insufficient Flux)\n- **No flashing animation** or pulsing effect is implemented\n\n### 4. Animation Implementation Approach\n**Status: CANVAS-BASED RENDERING**\n\n- **Current rendering**: All cell rendering is done using HTML5 Canvas (`CanvasGrid.tsx`)\n- **No CSS-based cell animations**: Cells are drawn directly on canvas context (lines 94-104)\n- **No requestAnimationFrame or animation loop** for cell transitions\n- **Canvas drawing approach** (lines 82-107 of `CanvasGrid.tsx`):\n  ```typescript\n  ctx.save()\n  ctx.shadowColor = color\n  ctx.shadowBlur = blur\n  ctx.fillStyle = color\n  ctx.beginPath()\n  ctx.roundRect(x + 1, y + 1, actualCellSize - 2, actualCellSize - 2, radius)\n  ctx.fill()\n  ctx.restore()\n  ```\n\n## Current Visual Feedback Implementation\n\n### What IS Implemented:\n1. **Age-based cell colors and glow effects** (canvas-based, static)\n   - Different colors for different cell ages (0-5+)\n   - Shadow blur effects based on cell age\n2. **Ghost cell preview** when hovering over grid\n   - Shows cyan (#00ffff) for placeable cells\n   - Shows magenta (#ff00ff) for removable cells\n   - Shows red (#ff0000) for invalid actions (insufficient Flux)\n3. **Cursor state changes** based on phase and Flux\n   - Crosshair for placeable/removable cells\n   - Not-allowed when interaction disabled\n4. **Flux counter color coding** (static transitions)\n   - Green/Yellow when plenty remaining\n   - Orange when <30% remaining\n   - Red when 0 remaining\n\n### What is NOT Implemented:\n1. **Cell placement fade-in animation** (0.1s)\n2. **Cell removal shrink animation** (0.15s)\n3. **Red flash animation** for invalid actions\n4. **Smooth value transitions** for Flux counter (mentioned in implementation plan line 217)\n\n## Implementation Plan Status\n\nAccording to `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`:\n- **Sprint 1.9** (Grid Interaction) - Cell animations marked as TODO (lines 235-238)\n- **Sprint 4.2** (Visual Polish) - Cell animations listed as MEDIUM priority (lines 632-635):\n  - Fade-in animation (0.1s) for placement\n  - Shrink animation (0.15s) for removal\n  - Use CSS transitions or canvas-based animations\n\n## Recommendation\n\nCell animations are **planned but not yet implemented**. The current implementation provides:\n- Instant state changes when placing/removing cells\n- Static visual feedback (red border) for invalid actions\n- No transition animations or effects\n\nTo implement cell animations, the project would need to add:\n1. An animation system (either CSS-based overlays or canvas-based interpolation)\n2. State tracking for animating cells (cell positions, sizes, opacity)\n3. Animation timing logic (requestAnimationFrame or CSS transitions)\n4. Integration with the existing canvas rendering pipeline\n\nThe implementation plan suggests these animations should be added in **Sprint 4.2** (Visual Polish), which comes after the core gameplay features are complete.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore cell animations implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef2d6ffe5Zm8B39Zp6e53B","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170762021,"end":1771170861019}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771170862837,"sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","part":{"id":"prt_c62010ce6001S0UnOfSurX7lrR","sessionID":"ses_39dff520effeHkWM6dK4B6huRO","messageID":"msg_c6200e3b40014xKbzfd4Mr5Evb","type":"tool","callID":"call_7386db58d5eb44619d97b44f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore level progression implementation","prompt":"Explore if level progression has been implemented. I need to check:\n1. Is there a level.ts file in src/lib/?\n2. Is level state managed anywhere (currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, etc.)?\n3. Are there any level configuration interfaces or types?\n4. Does the game handle multiple levels or just a single level?\n\nReturn a detailed summary of level progression implementation status."},"output":"task_id: ses_39dfef30affewb7vHEm3ZKpL4j (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's a detailed summary of the level progression implementation status:\n\n## Level Progression Implementation Status\n\n### 1. Level.ts File in src/lib/\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n- No `level.ts` file exists in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/`\n- The lib directory contains 18 files, none of which handle level logic\n\n### 2. Level State Management\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\nThe following state variables are completely absent from the codebase:\n- `currentLevel` - Not tracked anywhere\n- `maxUnlockedLevel` - Not tracked anywhere\n- `totalScore` - Not tracked across levels (only current score exists in scoring.ts)\n- Level progression state - Does not exist\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Searched for patterns: `currentLevel`, `maxUnlockedLevel`, `levelState` - **0 matches**\n- The main game state is managed in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` with only these state variables:\n  - `gridPreset` (SMALL/MEDIUM/LARGE)\n  - `grid` (the grid itself)\n  - `flux` (current resource budget)\n  - `phase` (PLANNING/COUNTDOWN/RUNNING/FINISHED)\n  - `showGridLines` (boolean)\n  - `interactionMode` (DRAW/ERASE)\n\n### 3. Level Configuration Interfaces/Types\n**Status: DEFINED BUT UNUSED**\n\nThe types ARE defined in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts` (lines 43-75):\n\n```typescript\nexport interface LevelConfig {\n  levelNumber: number\n  timeLimitSeconds: number\n  initialFlux: number\n}\n\nexport interface LevelProgression {\n  currentLevel: number\n  maxUnlockedLevel: number\n  totalScore: number\n  levels: LevelConfig[]\n}\n\nexport interface LevelGenerationParams {\n  baseTimeSeconds: number\n  timeIncrementPerLevel: number\n  baseFlux: number\n  difficultyScalingMode: DifficultyScalingMode\n}\n```\n\n**However:**\n- No code imports or uses these types\n- Searched for usage of `LevelConfig`, `LevelProgression`, `LevelGenerationParams` - **0 matches**\n- These are defined but never implemented\n\n### 4. Game Level Handling\n**Status: SINGLE LEVEL ONLY**\n\nThe game currently operates as a **single-level sandbox**:\n\n**Evidence from Game.tsx:**\n- No level selection or progression UI\n- No level counter display\n- No level completion or victory screens\n- Timer is hardcoded to a single phase duration\n- When FINISHED phase ends, it simply transitions back to PLANNING phase (see phase.ts line 26: `FINISHED: ['PLANNING']`)\n- Score resets on each new game (no accumulation)\n\n**Phase state machine (phase.ts):**\n```typescript\nconst PHASE_TRANSITIONS: Record<GamePhase, GamePhase[]> = {\n  PLANNING: ['COUNTDOWN'],\n  COUNTDOWN: ['RUNNING'],\n  RUNNING: ['FINISHED'],\n  FINISHED: ['PLANNING'],  // <-- Loops back to start, no level advancement\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Existing Infrastructure (Ready but Not Used)\n\nThe codebase has infrastructure that COULD support level progression:\n\n**Existing:**\n- ✅ Type definitions for levels\n- ✅ Scoring system (scoring.ts) - accumulates points\n- ✅ Phase management (phase.ts) - handles game flow\n- ✅ Flux management (flux.ts) - handles resource budgets\n- ✅ Timer system in phase.ts - handles countdowns\n- ✅ localStorage utilities (state.ts) - for persistence\n- ✅ Comprehensive spec document (specs/level-progression.md)\n\n**Missing:**\n- ❌ Level configuration generation logic\n- ❌ Level state management\n- ❌ Level transition system\n- ❌ Victory/end-of-game screen\n- ❌ Level UI display\n- ❌ Score accumulation across levels\n\n### 6. Implementation Plan Status\n\nFrom `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (lines 507-531):\n- Sprint 3.1 \"Level Progression\" is listed as **[ ] NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n- It's marked as HIGH priority but hasn't been started\n- The plan calls for a `src/lib/level.ts` file that doesn't exist\n\n### Summary\n\n**Level progression is NOT implemented.** The game is currently a single-level sandbox where players:\n1. Place cells with Flux budget\n2. Start simulation\n3. Watch the simulation run for a timer duration\n4. When finished, reset to PLANNING phase and start over\n\nThe types and specifications exist (planned but not implemented), but none of the actual level progression logic has been coded. The foundation is there (scoring, phases, timers, storage), but it would require significant development to implement the full level progression system as outlined in the spec.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore level progression implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39dfef30affewb7vHEm3ZKpL4j","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771170761970,"end":1771170862835}}}}
